2,Naueti language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Naueti_language,"January 17, 2026 - Naueti (also written as Nauoti, Nauete and Nauweti but ultimately from Naueti nau eti 'now') is an Austronesian language spoken by 15,045 (census 2010) in the subdistricts of Uato-Lari, Uatucarbau and Baguia in southeastern East Timor.",Nauete,Austronesian
3,Ministry of Culture-Austronesian Music and Cultural Exchange,https://www.moc.gov.tw/en/cp.aspx?n=443,"It's a pity that Taiwanese aboriginal songs are rich and various yet there are only a few musical instruments. I found a few and compare them with the ones from Southeast Asia. We all know that twin-pipe nose flutes are only found in Taiwan, and they exist in Paiwan and are documented in Tsou's literature. The Austronesians in Southeast Asia have single-pipe nose flutes instead of twin-pipe nose flutes.",Nauete,Austronesian
